{
  "tool_id": "art-772-daycount-year-fraction",
  "note": "SHARED-DAYCOUNT-BUNDLE-1 golden vectors. The six calendar _amort modes follow the ISDA 2006 Definitions Sec 4.16 clause formulas (hand-verified arithmetic: v1 29/360, v2 182/360 vs v3 181/360, v4 180/360 vs v5 179/360, v6 182/360, v7 366/365, v8 184/365+182/366, v9 29/366). ACT_ACT_ICMA follows ICMA Rule 251 as pinned in the node shard cited_clause_digest (days in accrual period / (days in reference period x frequency)); v11-v13 are its declared refusal branches. BUS_252 counts business days d1<d<=d2 over the caller calendar and divides by the fixed 252; the calendar (weekend + holidays) is hash-pinned caller data via policy_parameters, never kernel bytes (the _ruleversion single-writer ruling); this fixture set pins weekend+2026-01-01 (v14) and a 401-day holiday wall (v21). v18-v20 and v22 make the date/convention refusal branches reachable per AUTHORING-STANDARD Sec 1. output_payload values were generated by running this kernel's compute() over each policy_parameters; the proptest fixture-oracle and golden-parity re-derive them.",
